    "one_number": {
      "value": "$2.4 billion",
      "unit": "extra diesel cost this season",
      "context": "A Joint Economic Committee analysis by Democrats, released this month, put the added diesel cost to farmers at $2.4 billion for the 2025-2026 planting and harvest."
    },
    "sections": [
      {
        "title": "Grains bounce after a slide",
        "body": "- Dec corn is at **$4.51½** overnight, up 2¾ cents, after four straight lower closes.\n- Feedstuffs reported Tuesday that a swift harvest weighed on corn and soybeans, and winter wheat kept struggling.\n- Chicago wheat is at $6.12¼, up 2 cents.",
        "so_what": "A fast harvest keeps supply in front of the market.",
        "conviction_level": "low",
        "overnight_surprise": false
      },
      {
        "title": "Hogs fall, cattle hold",
        "body": "- Dec hogs settled Tuesday at **$62.025**, down from $64.675 Monday.\n- Feeder cattle settled up 0.8% at $352.80. Live cattle held at $230.00.\n- Smithfield said lower pork markets challenged its third quarter.",
        "so_what": "Pork margins are the soft spot in the meat complex.",
        "conviction_level": "low",
        "overnight_surprise": false
      },
      {
        "title": "Crude firm, gas gains",
        "body": "- WTI is at **$101.82** overnight, up 1.9%, after renewed Houthi attacks on Saudi Arabia, oilprice.com reported.\n- ING strategists say traders are positioning for fresh Iran hostilities after the Nov. 3 elections, and prices would likely drop if none come.\n- Natural gas is at $3.07, up 13.9% from Tuesday's $2.70 settle.",
        "so_what": "Diesel stays costly through the end of harvest.",
        "conviction_level": "medium",
        "overnight_surprise": true
      }
